<!-- ===== PRIMARY ENGAGEMENTS ===== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="label">engagement shapes</div>
    <h2>How the engagement shapes work.</h2>
    <p>Each shape is productized: fixed scope, fixed deliverables, written quote before signing. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Scoping Call</strong> is the entry (free, 30 min). <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Pilot Build</strong> when you want one working piece before committing to a full build. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Sprint</strong> when the workflow fits in one sentence. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Custom</strong> for anything multi-workflow. <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Ops Retainer</strong> for maintenance and tuning of systems already shipped. Every paid shape is quoted on scope before signing.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 00 · SCOPING CALL -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="scoping-call">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1"><span class="pulse"></span>00 · SCOPING CALL</div>
        <h3>A 30-minute call.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time">FREE · 30 MIN</div>
        <div class="slots">BY APPOINTMENT</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>I walk you through one workflow, sharpen scope, and decide which paid shape fits.</p>
        <p>If none does, I'll say so on the call and point you to who or what's better.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>ON THE CALL</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>What's broken, or what should ship next</li>
          <li>Honest read on whether AI is the fix</li>
          <li>If yes: which shape matches</li>
          <li>Rough scope + cost in writing within 24 hrs</li>
          <li>If no: referral or alternative</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FREE · REMOTE · 24-HR FOLLOW-UP</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 01 · PILOT BUILD -->
  <div class="tier-card featured reveal" id="pilot">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1"><span class="pulse"></span>01 · PILOT BUILD</div>
        <h3>One working piece, before the full build.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time">FIXED PRICE · ~2 DAYS</div>
        <div class="slots">$750 · CREDITED TO SPRINT</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>A small, fixed-price build. In a day or two I build one part of your workflow and get it running on your real data, so you can see how it works before paying for the full build.</p>
        <p><strong>Pilot vs Sprint:</strong> a Pilot builds one piece. A Sprint builds the complete, production-ready workflow: deployed to your infrastructure, documented, supported, and owned. The $750 Pilot fee comes off the Sprint price if you keep going, so it costs nothing extra to start small.</p>
        <p>A good fit when you want to see it work first, or a past tool didn't hold up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>One working part of your workflow, running on your real data</li>
          <li>Code in your repository, versioned in git</li>
          <li>A short Loom walkthrough of how it runs</li>
          <li>A written note on what the full Sprint would add</li>
          <li>Starts within a few days of signing</li>
          <li>$750 flat, credited toward a Sprint if you proceed</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">$750 · REMOTE · CREDITED TO SPRINT</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ START A PILOT</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 02 · SPRINT -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="sprint">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--red);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--red);"></span>02 · BUILD SPRINT</div>
        <h3>One workflow, shipped in a fixed window.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--red);">FROM $2,500 · FIXED-SCOPE BUILD</div>
        <div class="slots">50% UPFRONT</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-body">
      <div class="col">
        <h4>WHAT IT IS</h4>
        <p>The complete, production-ready build of one workflow, with a fixed scope and fixed delivery window. Agreed at signing, then deployed to your infrastructure, documented, and owned outright by the end of the sprint. Where a Pilot builds one piece, the Sprint builds the whole workflow.</p>
        <p>The workflow has to fit in one sentence, for example, "send a summary of yesterday's sign-ups to my inbox at 6am every weekday." If it can't, a Custom build is the right shape instead.</p>
        <p>Not ready to commit? Start with a <a href="/services/#pilot">$750 Pilot Build</a> and apply it toward the Sprint.</p>
        <p><strong>Common scopes:</strong> daily operational brief, weekly metrics report, sales follow-up automation, content cross-poster, AI-assisted inbox triage.</p>
        <p><strong>Fixed-price sprints:</strong> <a href="/services/sprints/geo/">GEO / AI-search ($2,500)</a>, <a href="/services/sprints/mcp-server/">MCP server ($3,500)</a>, <a href="/services/sprints/programmatic-seo/">programmatic SEO ($4,500)</a>, <a href="/services/sprints/lead-pipeline/">lead pipeline ($4,500)</a>. Anything off this list is quoted on scope.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h4>DELIVERABLES</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>A single workflow with a defined input and output</li>
          <li>Deployment on the client's Vercel account (or mine, transferred at close)</li>
          <li>README, cost projection, and environment-variable specification</li>
          <li>15-minute handoff walkthrough on Loom plus an architecture diagram</li>
          <li>14 days of post-sprint bug fixes included</li>
          <li>Full code ownership at the close of the engagement</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-foot">
      <span class="meta">FROM $2,500 · 50% UPFRONT · 14-DAY FIX WINDOW</span>
      <a href="/contact/">→ BOOK SPRINT CALL</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 03 · CUSTOM -->
  <div class="tier-card reveal" id="custom">
    <div class="tier-head">
      <div class="left">
        <div class="row1" style="color: var(--blue);"><span class="pulse" style="background: var(--blue);"></span>03 · CUSTOM BUILD</div>
        <h3>Multi-workflow builds.</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <div class="time" style="color: var(--blue);">QUOTE-BASED</div>
        <div class="slots">MILESTONE-PAID</div>
